CYBERSECURITY AND INFRASTRUCTURE SECURITY AGENCY
NATIONAL CYBERSECURITY ADVISORY AA26-260A

SUMMARY:
Vulnerability: CVE-2023-44487
Vendor: Apache Software Foundation / Cloud Infrastructure Providers
Product: Apache HTTP Server & Reverse Proxies
Affected Versions: All implementations supporting HTTP/2 prior to October 2023 patches
Vulnerability Type: Distributed Denial of Service / Resource Exhaustion
Attack Vector: NETWORK
MITRE ATT&CK Technique: T1498 (Network Denial of Service)
Exploitation Status: CONFIRMED_EXPLOITATION_IN_WILD
Attack Outcome: EXPLOITED_SUCCESSFULLY
Affected Sector: Cloud Services, Financial Platforms, E-Commerce
Publication Date: 2026-09-17

TECHNICAL ANALYSIS:
Attackers exploit the HTTP/2 stream cancellation mechanism by sending a barrage of HEADERS frames followed immediately by RST_STREAM frames. This overwhelms public load balancers and web servers without saturating link bandwidth, causing widespread service disruption across cloud workloads.

REQUIRED DIRECTIVES:
- Enable rate limiting on stream resets and apply vendor patches on reverse proxy tiers.
- CIS Control 4.1: Deploy Layer 7 Web Application Firewall (WAF) mitigations.

FINANCIAL IMPACT:
Downtime and incident response costs estimated at ₹2,900,000 for critical customer-facing portals.

Confidence: 0.93
